PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F405A1786745066
OL,3,C'A wildlife emergency': Hundreds of
OL,4,Cfish die in muddy pond
OL,6,F"While we are unable to carry out fish
OL,7,Frescues from ornamental ponds, we are
OL,8,Falways willing to give advice to
OL,9,Fowners on the best way to safely and
OL,10,Flegally mind their stock.
OL,12,F"Those responsible for fish need to
OL,13,Ftake utmost care when moving them to
OL,14,Fother waters. Diseased fish can
OL,15,Fdevastate entire populations if moved
OL,16,Fto new waters, and predators can pose
OL,17,Fa further threat."
OL,19,FThe agency introducing any fish to
OL,20,Fopen waters needs its approval first.
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@AOUyD@RO]
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G7/8
